# Backend change cases (PetWell)

New product APIs live in **petwell-api** (HTTP + Dynamo). Do not add `@model` / `@function` to Amplify GraphQL for new work.

## Do not (default)

- Edit `amplify/backend/api/clientGraph/schema.graphql`
- Run `amplify push` of the GraphQL API
- Add console GSIs on `*-{apiId}-prod` Amplify tables
- Trust `userId` / `authorId` from the JSON body — use Cognito JWT `sub`
- Put Vercel functions in US East; use **sin1**. Dynamo is `ap-southeast-1`

## Legacy Lambda bugfix

Code-only: `amplify function push <functionName>` or zip + `aws lambda update-function-code`. Not a full API push.

IAM/env on that function: that function’s stack only.

GraphQL **signature** change (new args on `@function`): still needs schema push — avoid by putting the new field on petwell-api HTTP instead.

## Case A — new field, HTTP-only

`UpdateItem` the attribute on the existing table. No Amplify. GraphQL clients ignore unknown attributes.

## Case B — GraphQL clients must read the field

Last resort: add the field in `schema.graphql` + `amplify push`, **only if the human explicitly asks**. Prefer Case A + HTTP.

## Case C — need to query/filter by a new field on an Amplify table

Prefer a **new table you own**. Otherwise `@index` in schema + push. Never add a GSI in the AWS console on Amplify-owned tables (CloudFormation drift).

## New table

Create `PetWell…` in `ap-southeast-1` yourself. Never `@model`. petwell-api owns it.

## Auth

Cognito ID token `Authorization: Bearer …`. Identity = `payload.sub`. Admin = `cognito:groups` contains `Admin`. Partner hub uses HMAC sessions in `partnerAuth`, not this API’s Cognito path.

## Docs

Update `docs/ai/` in the same session (`Last updated` UTC+8).
